@startuml
' Class diagram decomposing the Common module's Domain Model (Figure 8).
' Authored in issue #9. Renders through scripts/render-diagrams.sh.
' The catalog uses the GoF Composite pattern: CatalogItem is the component, Product the
' leaf, ProductFamily the composite, and totalValue() is the recursive operation.
' Every association carries multiplicities; the key names each relation type.
!include style.puml
title Domain model: class diagram of the Common module

skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #203864
  AttributeFontColor #15243B
}
skinparam nodesep 16
skinparam ranksep 32

together {
  abstract class CatalogItem {
    totalValue(): Money
  }
  class Product {
    id
    name
    unitValue
  }
  class ProductFamily {
    name
  }
}

abstract class StockHolder {
  id
  name
}
class Store
class DistributionCenter

class InventoryLevel {
  quantity
}
class InventoryEvent {
  id
  sequence
  delta
  timestamp
  type
}
class ShippingOrder {
  id
  status
}
class ShippingOrderLine {
  quantity
}
together {
  class Report {
    generatedAt
  }
  enum ReportType {
    LowestStock
    OverstockedItems
    ProductFamilyTotalValue
  }
}

' ---- GoF Composite: the product catalog ----------------------------------------
CatalogItem <|-- Product
CatalogItem <|-- ProductFamily
ProductFamily "0..*" o-- "0..*" CatalogItem : contains >
note top of CatalogItem
  GoF Composite pattern: CatalogItem is the component,
  Product the leaf, ProductFamily the composite;
  totalValue() is the recursive operation. A product may
  belong to several families (many-to-many); the family
  total-value report counts it once per family.
end note

' ---- holders and the stock they carry ------------------------------------------
StockHolder <|-- Store
StockHolder <|-- DistributionCenter
StockHolder "1" o-- "0..*" InventoryLevel : holds >
InventoryLevel "0..*" --> "1" Product : of >

' ---- events reference their source holder and product --------------------------
InventoryEvent "0..*" --> "1" StockHolder : source >
InventoryEvent "0..*" --> "1" Product : product >

' ---- shipping orders: raised at a store, fulfilled by the DC --------------------
Store "1" --> "0..*" ShippingOrder : raises >
ShippingOrder "0..*" --> "1" DistributionCenter : to >
ShippingOrder "1" *-- "1..*" ShippingOrderLine : lines >
ShippingOrderLine "0..*" --> "1" Product : item >

' ---- reports: one of three kinds; the family-value report scopes a family -------
Report "0..*" --> "1" ReportType : kind >
Report "0..*" ..> "0..1" ProductFamily : scopes >

legend right
|= Notation |= Meaning |
| class box | a domain type in the Domain Model module |
| triangle (hollow) | generalization (is-a) |
| open diamond | aggregation (whole has parts) |
| filled diamond | composition (whole owns its parts) |
| solid arrow | association; label names the role, numbers are multiplicities |
| dashed arrow | dependency (uses) |
| <<enumeration>> | a fixed set of values |
endlegend
@enduml
